An alias names a server endpoint and its credentials. The configuration file
is ~/.nexoctl/config.json (or $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR/config.json, or --config-dir),
written with owner-only permissions (0600).

Usage:
  nexoctl alias [flags]
  nexoctl alias [command]

Available Commands:
  list        List aliases (secret keys are never shown)
  remove      Remove an alias
  set         Add or update an alias

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for alias

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl alias [command] --help" for more information about a command.
